        "judgment": "supported descriptive comparison",
        "evidence": "Three independent teams interviewed 79 households about ostrich conservation in Zimbabwe, 123 respondents about wolves in Pakistan and 343 households about carnivores in Ethiopia. All measured attitudes towards local wildlife. The Zimbabwe study reports the importance of conservation and willingness to report sightings. The other two report predominantly negative attitudes toward wolves or carnivore conservation in their respective samples. The survey questions, response scales and species differ. Compare the local findings qualitatively. A pooled attitude percentage has no common denominator across these instruments.",
